'' TKO0997: 'win.MsgBox' is sys/win's MsgBox function, a procedure and not a type. It declared
'' a 4-byte variable; spell the struct tagMSG (or MSG with the program's own
'' '#include "windows.bi"'). The test named 'win.MSG', sys/win's Msg function until it became
'' MsgBox -- that now names nothing in win, which is TKO0808. sys/win declares generics, so
'' this unit is walked twice (genericdiscover.tiko), and TKO0997's once-per-node guard, the
'' ref the first walk set, silenced the second: neither line was reported once Msg was gone.
'' TEST: cli
'' NEEDS: toolchains/tiko-windows/inc
''     (named by -i below)
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -c -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/modules/src/taskswin/win-msg-qualified.tiko -o tests/modules/src/taskswin/win-msg-qualified.o
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: win-msg-qualified.tiko(4,10): error TKO0997: 'win.msgbox' is a procedure, not a type
'' EXPECT-OUT: win-msg-qualified.tiko(5,10): error TKO0808: the type 'win.msg' is not declared
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 2
